    "seccion": "Inoperative Equipment",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "What action should be taken if one of the two VHF radios fail while IFR in controlled airspace?",
    "options": [
      "Notify ATC immediately.",
      "Squawk 7600.",
      "Monitor the VOR receiver."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The pilot-in-command of an aircraft operating IFR in controlled airspace shall report to ATC as soon as practical any malfunction of navigational, approach or communication equipment that occurs in flight. (PLT162, AA.VI.D.K3) — 14 CFR §91.187 Answer (B) is incorrect because, although you have experienced a communications failure, it is only a partial one. You still have one operational VHF radio and all other radios are working normally, so a squawk of 7600 is not needed. Answer (C) is incorrect because you still have an operable VHF radio for communication, so monitoring of a NAVAID is not needed. The only pilot action required is notification to ATC of the problem.",
