  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9258",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Communications",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "ATC asks you to follow the B737 3 NM ahead of you on the approach path. ATC is responsible to ensure",
    "options": [
      "wake turbulence avoidance.",
      "traffic separation only.",
      "wind shear avoidance."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "A pilot’s acceptance of instructions to follow another aircraft or provide visual separation from it is an acknowledgment that the pilot will maneuver the aircraft as necessary to avoid the other aircraft or to maintain in-trail separation. In operations conducted behind heavy jet aircraft, it is also an acknowledgment that the pilot accepts the responsibility for wake turbulence separation. (PLT149, AA.II.C.K6) — AIM ¶4-4-14",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-17 · question 9258 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9258",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
