  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9783_1",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Communications",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "If you notice ATC is unusually quiet and one of your VHF transmit lights is illuminated, then you should suspect",
    "options": [
      "your VHF receiver is inoperative.",
      "your VHF transmitter is keyed and you probably have a stuck microphone.",
      "the radio is performing a self-test function."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "If radio communications are unusually quiet, suspect radio problems or a stuck microphone, and then contact ATC and look for light gun signals. (PLT542, AA.I.A.K9) — AC 120-74",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-17 · question 9783-1 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
