  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8999",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Horizontal Situation Indicator (HSI)",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figures 142 and 143.) To which aircraft position does HSI presentation “D” correspond?",
    "options": [
      "4.",
      "15.",
      "17."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "HSI Indicator “D” has a course selection of 180°, and the TO/FROM indicator is pointing to the tail of the course arrow. So the aircraft is flying away FROM the station, and is south of R-270 and R-090. The CDI bar is deflected left, which means the aircraft is west of R-180. The aircraft heading is 180°, which describes position 17. (PLT355, AA.VI.D.K3) — FAA-H-8083-15 Answer (A) is incorrect because position 4 is to the north of the 270/090 radials, which would require a TO indication. Answer (B) is incorrect because the course deflection bar on position 15 would have a centered deflection bar and a heading of 360°.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-24 · question 8999 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
    "sourceQuestionId": "8999",
