  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8986",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Horizontal Situation Indicator (HSI)",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 139.) Which OBS selection on the No. 1 NAV would center the CDI and change the ambiguity indication to a TO?",
    "options": [
      "175.",
      "165.",
      "345."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The No. 1 Nav has a course selection of 350°, and the TO/FROM indicator is pointing to the tail of the course arrow. So the aircraft is flying away FROM the station, and is in the north hemisphere. The CDI bar is deflected 2.5° right and the aircraft heading is 140°, which would put the aircraft on R-345. To center the CDI and change the ambiguity indication to a TO, rotate the OBS to 165° (the reciprocal of R-345). (PLT276, AA.VI.D.K3) — FAA-H-8083-15 Answers (A) and (C) are incorrect because the aircraft is currently on R-345.",
