    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Full scale deflection is 10°, so each dot represents 2°. The CDI is displaced two dots (4°). The OBS is set at 170° with a FROM indication, and the aircraft is 4° to the right of course (or on R-174). Simply rotating the OBS to 174° would center the CDI. (PLT276, AA.VI.D.K3) — FAA-H-8083-15 Answer (B) is incorrect because a right deflection would indicate R-166. Answer (C) is incorrect because the TO-FROM indicator is on FROM, not TO.",
