    "text": "When is the course deviation indicator (CDI) considered to have a full-scale deflection?",
    "options": [
      "When the CDI deflects from full-scale left to full-scale right, or vice versa.",
      "When the CDI deflects from the center of the scale to full-scale left or right.",
      "When the CDI deflects from half-scale left to halfscale right, or vice versa."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Full-scale deflection is 5 dots to either side of center. (PLT276, AA.VI.E.K2) — FAA-H-8083-15 Answers (A) and (C) are incorrect because when the CDI deflects full-scale left to full-scale right (or vice versa), this represents 2 full-scale deflections.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-33 · question 8968 · ALL",
