  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8969",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Approach Systems",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Which “rule-of-thumb” may be used to approximate the rate of descent required for a 3° glidepath?",
    "options": [
      "5 times groundspeed in knots.",
      "8 times groundspeed in knots.",
      "10 times groundspeed in knots."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The descent rate in feet per minute required to maintain a 3° glide slope is roughly five times your ground speed in knots. (PLT170, AA.VI.E.K4) — FAA-P-8740-48 Answer (B) is incorrect because 8 times the ground speed in knots would result in a 5% glide slope. Answer (C) is incorrect because 10 times the ground speed in knots would result in a 6% glide slope.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-33 · question 8969 · ALL",
