    "seccion": "Approach Systems",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 253.) You are cleared to LXV in your helicopter and expect to be given the GPS RWY 16 approach. Your helicopter is equipped with an IFR certified WAAS GPS. Your approach minimums will be",
    "options": [
      "11,360' MDA and 3/4 mi.",
      "11,360' MDA and 1-1/4 mi.",
      "11,360' MDA and 6,600 RVR, or 1-1/2 mi."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Helicopters flying conventional (non-helicopter) SIAPs may reduce the visibility minima to not less than one half the published Category A landing visibility minima, or 1/4 SM visibility/1200 RVR, whichever is greater unless the procedure is annotated with “Visibility Reduction by Helicopters NA.” (PLT354) — AIM ¶10-1-2",
