    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Approach Systems",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 250.) You arrive at DUMBB for the RNAV (GPS) at CHA. Before takeoff, the preflight briefer states WAAS may be unreliable. Your avionics are good and you have full GPS service. You",
    "options": [
      "can descend to the LNAV MDA of 1,200 feet and 2,400 RVR due to the FSS advisory.",
      "descend to the LPV minima of 882 feet and 2,400 RVR in your CAT B aircraft.",
      "can descend to the LNAV MDA of 518 feet due to the FSS advisory."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Upon commencing an approach at locations with a “WAAS MAY NOT BE AVBL” NOTAM, if the WAAS avionics indicate LNAV/VNAV or LPV service is available, then vertical guidance may be used to complete the approach using the displayed level of service. (PLT354, AA.VI.E.K2) — AIM ¶1-1-18",
