  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9429",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Global Positioning System (GPS)",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "If Receiver Autonomous Integrity Monitoring (RAIM) is not available when setting up for GPS approach, the pilot should",
    "options": [
      "continue to the MAP and hold until the satellites are recaptured.",
      "proceed as cleared to the IAF and hold until satellite reception is satisfactory.",
      "select another type of approach using another type of navigation aid."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "If RAIM is not available, another type of navigation and approach system must be used, another destination selected, or the trip delayed until RAIM is predicted to be available on arrival. (PLT354, AA.VI.D.K2) — AIM ¶1-1-17",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-37 · question 9429 · ALL",
