    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Airport Lighting and Marking",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 129.) What is the runway distance remaining at “A” for a daytime takeoff on Runway 9?",
    "options": [
      "1,000 feet.",
      "1,500 feet.",
      "2,000 feet."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The fixed distance marker is located 1,000 feet from the threshold (in this case the end of the runway). (PLT141, AA.II.C.K3) — AIM ¶2-3-3 Answer (B) is incorrect because the 1,500 feet distance of runway remaining is not marked on an FAA nonprecision runway. Answer (C) is incorrect because 2,000 feet is the distance remaining on an ICAO (not FAA) nonprecision instrument runway where the runway edge lights are amber.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-47 · question 8922 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
