    "seccion": "Airport Lighting and Marking",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "When conducting land and hold short operations (LAHSO), the pilot should have readily available:",
    "options": [
      "the published available landing distance (ALD), landing performance of the aircraft, and slope of all LAHSO combinations at the destination airport.",
      "the published runway length and slope for all LAHSO combinations at the airport of intended landing.",
      "the landing performance of the aircraft, published available landing distance (ALD) for all LAHSO combinations at the airport of intended landing, plus the forecast winds."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "To conduct LAHSO, pilots should become familiar with all available information concerning LAHSO at their destination airport. Pilots should have, readily available, the published ALD and runway slope information for all LAHSO runway combinations at each airport of intended landing. Additionally, knowledge about landing performance data permits the pilot to readily determine that the ALD for the assigned runway is sufficient for safe LAHSO. (PLT140, AA.VI.F.R3b) — AIM ¶4-3-11",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-49 · question 9733 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9733",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 49,
    "sourceCategories": [
      "ATM",
      "ATS",
      "RTC"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9734",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Airport Lighting and Marking",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "The airport markings, signage and lighting associated with land and hold short (LAHSO) consists of:",
    "options": [
      "yellow hold-short markings, red and white signage, and in-pavement lights.",
      "red and white signage, yellow hold-short markings, and at some airports, in-pavement lights.",
      "red and black signage, in-pavement lights, and yellow hold-short markings."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The airport markings, signage, and lighting associated with LAHSO consist of a three-part system of yellow hold short markings, red and white signage, and, in certain cases, in-pavement lighting. (PLT140, AA.VI.F.R3b) — AIM ¶4-3-11",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-49 · question 9734 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
