    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Airport Lighting and Marking",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "The ILS critical area sign indicates",
    "options": [
      "where aircraft are prohibited.",
      "the edge of the ILS critical area.",
      "the exit boundary."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The ILS critical area sign is located adjacent to the ILS holding position marking on the pavement and can be seen by pilots leaving the critical area. The sign is intended to provide pilots with another visual cue to use as a guide in deciding when they are clear of the ILS critical area. (PLT141, AA.II.C.S3) — AIM ¶2-3-9",
