  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9423_1",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Airport Lighting and Marking",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 227.) The “taxiway ending” marker",
    "options": [
      "identifies area where aircraft are prohibited.",
      "indicates taxiway does not continue.",
      "provides general taxiing direction to named taxiway."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Taxiway ending marker is an airport sign indicating the taxiway does not continue. (PLT141, AA.II.C.K3) — AIM ¶2-3-11 Answer (A) is incorrect because this is the purpose of a no entry sign. Answer (C) is incorrect because this is the purpose of direction signs.",
