      "1 dashed and 1 solid yellow line."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Holding position markings for taxiway/runway intersections consist of four yellow lines—two solid and two dashed. The solid lines are always on the same side where the aircraft is to hold. (PLT149, AA.II.C.K3) — AIM ¶2-3-5",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-50 · question 8203 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
