    "sourceCategories": [
      "ATM",
      "ATS",
      "RTC"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8908",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 2,
    "capituloTitulo": "Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities",
    "seccion": "Approach Lighting",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "What are the indications of precision approach path indicator (PAPI)?",
    "options": [
      "High – white; on glidepath – red and white; low – red.",
      "High – white; on glidepath – green; low – red.",
      "High – white and green; on glidepath – green; low – red."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The PAPI uses light units similar to the VASI but are installed in a single row of either two or four light units: High ........................................................4 white lights Slightly high ..................................1 red, 3 white lights On glide path ................................2 red, 2 white lights Slightly low ...................................1 white, 3 red lights Low ............................................................4 red lights (PLT147, AA.III.B.K4) — AIM ¶2-1-2 Answer (B) is incorrect because the on glidepath indication of PAPI is both red and white lights. Answer (C) is incorrect because above the glidepath indication of PAPI is all white, on glidepath is two red and two white, and below glidepath is all red.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 2 Equipment, Navigation, and Facilities · p. 2-55 · question 8908 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
    "sourceQuestionId": "8908",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 55,
    "sourceCategories": [
