  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9813_1",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Critical Engine and VMC",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "High density altitude can reduce turbojet aircraft performance in which of the following ways?",
    "options": [
      "It reduces the likelihood of maintaining laminar flow over the airfoils as airspeed and altitude increase.",
      "It reduces thrust because there is a reduced mass of gases to force out of the exhaust.",
      "It reduces thrust because there is an increased mass of gases that inhibits the outflow of exhaust."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The engine’s compressor section has to work harder when air density is decreased. Power capability is reduced at high density altitudes, and power use may have to be modulated to keep engine temperature within limits. (PLT005, AA.I.B.K3a) — FAA-H-8083-3",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-9 · question 9813-1 · ATM, ATS",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9813-1",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
