    "explanation": "Due to the increased load factor in a coordinated turn, there will be an increase in stall speed and—of greater importance to engine-out performance—an increase in induced drag. A bank angle of 15° will increase induced drag by about 7 percent. (PLT237, AA.IV.A.K2d) — ANA",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-12 · question 8345-2 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
