    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Stability",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "An airplane loaded with the CG aft of the rearCG limit could",
    "options": [
      "make it easier to recover from stalls and spins.",
      "make it more difficult to flare for landing.",
      "increase the likelihood of inadvertent overstress."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "If an airplane is loaded too far rearward, it may not dampen out a vertical displacement of the nose. Instead, when the nose is momentarily pulled up, such as when flaring for landing, it may alternately climb and dive becoming steeper with each oscillation. (PLT240, AA.I.B.K5) — FAA-H-8083-25",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-14 · question 9921 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9921",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
