      "ATS",
      "ADX"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8387",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "High Speed Flight",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Within what Mach range does transonic flight regimes usually occur?",
    "options": [
      ".50 to .75 Mach.",
      ".75 to 1.20 Mach.",
      "1.20 to 2.50 Mach."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Flight regimes are defined as follows: Subsonic – Mach numbers below 0.75 Transonic – Mach numbers from 0.75 to 1.20 Supersonic – Mach numbers from 1.20 to 5.00 Hypersonic – Mach numbers above 5.00. (PLT032, AA.I.D.K1) — ANA Answer (A) is incorrect because .50 to .75 Mach would be subsonic flight. Answer (C) is incorrect because 1.20 to 2.50 Mach would be supersonic flight.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-16 · question 8387 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
