  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8325",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Primary Flight Controls",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "When are outboard ailerons normally used?",
    "options": [
      "Low-speed flight only.",
      "High-speed flight only.",
      "Low-speed and high-speed flight."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "At high speeds, flaps are retracted and the outboard ailerons are locked out of the aileron control system. (PLT346, AA.I.A.K12) — FAA-H-8083-25 Answers (B) and (C) are incorrect because the outboard ailerons are locked when airspeed is increased and flaps are raised.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-20 · question 8325 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
