      "ADX"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8333",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Primary Flight Controls",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "For which purpose may flight spoilers be used?",
    "options": [
      "Reduce the wings’ lift upon landing.",
      "Increase the rate of descent without increasing aerodynamic drag.",
      "Aid in longitudinal balance when rolling an airplane into a turn."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "An additional purpose or use for flight spoilers is to re duce lift when the aircraft lands. (PLT473, AA.I.A.K12) — FAA-H-8083-25 Answer (B) is incorrect because spoilers will increase the aerodynamic drag. Answer (C) is incorrect because trim devices (not spoilers) aid in balancing forces on an aircraft about the three axes.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-21 · question 8333 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
    "sourceQuestionId": "8333",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
