      "ATS",
      "ADX"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9793",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Primary Flight Controls",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Upon landing, spoilers",
    "options": [
      "decrease directional stability on the landing rollout.",
      "function by increasing tire to ground friction.",
      "should be extended after the thrust reversers have been deployed."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Spoilers should be deployed immediately after touch-down because they are most effective at high speed. The spoilers increase wheel loading by as much as 200 percent in the landing flap configuration. This increases the tire ground friction force making the maximum tire braking and cornering forces available. (PLT170, AA.I.A.K12) — FAA-H-8083-3A",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-21 · question 9793 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9793",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 21,
    "sourceCategories": [
