      "ADX"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9793_1",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Primary Flight Controls",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Aerodynamic braking is only effective up to approximately",
    "options": [
      "30% of touchdown speed.",
      "40 to 50% of touchdown speed.",
      "60 to 70% of touchdown speed."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "The aerodynamic drag of the airplane must be considered during the landing roll. Because of the reduced induced drag when in ground effect, aerodynamic braking will be of greatest significance only when partial stalling of the wing can be accomplished. The reduced drag when in ground effect accounts for the fact that the brakes are the most effective source of deceleration for the majority of airplane configurations. At speeds less than 60 to 70 percent of the touchdown speed, aerodynamic drag is so slight as to be of little use, and therefore aerodynamic braking must be utilized to produce continued deceleration of the airplane. (PLT247, AA.I.A.K12) — ANA",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-21 · question 9793-1 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9793-1",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 21,
    "sourceCategories": [
      "ATM",
      "ATS",
      "ADX"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": []
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9793_2",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Primary Flight Controls",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Ground spoilers used after landing are",
    "options": [
      "more effective at low speed.",
      "equally effective at any speed.",
      "more effective at high speed."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Spoilers should be deployed immediately after touch-down because they are most effective at high speed. (PLT473, AA.I.A.K12) — FAA-H-8083-3",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-21 · question 9793-2 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9793-2",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
