    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Anti-servo tabs move in the same direction as the primary control surface. (PLT346, AA.I.A.K12) — FAA-H-8083-25 Answer (B) is incorrect because a servo tab moves in the opposite direction from the primary control surface. Answer (C) is incorrect because trim tabs remain fixed during control inputs.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-24 · question 8337 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
