    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The primary purpose of high-lift devices (flaps, slots, slats, etc.) is to increase the CL of the airplane and to MAX reduce the stall speed. The takeoff and landing speeds are consequently reduced. (PLT305, AA.I.A.K12) — ANA Answer (B) is incorrect because, to decrease the rate of sink, the CL must increase. This is done by using leading-edge lift devices, slats, flaps, and other devices with the correct power setting. Answer (C) is incorrect because spoilers increase profile drag and are usually deployed after touchdown to reduce lift.",
