  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8386",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "High-Lift Devices",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "What effect does the leading edge slot in the wing have on performance?",
    "options": [
      "Decreases profile drag.",
      "Changes the stalling angle of attack to a higher angle.",
      "Decelerates the upper surface boundary layer air."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The slot delays stall to a higher angle of attack. (PLT305, AA.I.A.K12) — ANA Answer (A) is incorrect because, at low angles of attack, there is little or no profile drag increase. At high angles of attack, the slot delays the stall characteristics of the wing. Answer (C) is incorrect because the leading-edge slot actually increases airflow on the upper wing surface to allow higher angles of attack.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-26 · question 8386 · ATM, ATS, ADX",
