  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8409",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Helicopter Aerodynamics",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "During a hover, a helicopter tends to drift in the direction of tail rotor thrust. What is this movement called?",
    "options": [
      "Translating tendency.",
      "Transverse flow effect.",
      "Gyroscopic precession."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The entire helicopter has a tendency to move in the direction of tail rotor thrust when hovering, which is often referred to as drift or translating tendency. (PLT268) — FAA-H-8083-21",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-28 · question 8409 · RTC",
