  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9831",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 3,
    "capituloTitulo": "Aerodynamics",
    "seccion": "Helicopter Aerodynamics",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "A level attitude in flight in a helicopter indicates",
    "options": [
      "acceleration.",
      "descent.",
      "stable flight."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "In straight-and-level unaccelerated forward flight, lift equals weight and thrust equals drag (straight-and-level flight is flight with a constant heading and at a constant altitude). If lift exceeds weight, the helicopter climbs; if lift is less than weight, the helicopter descends. If thrust exceeds drag, the helicopter speeds up; if thrust is less than drag, it slows down. (PLT219) — FAA-H-8083-21",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 3 Aerodynamics · p. 3-30 · question 9831 · RTC",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9831",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 30,
    "sourceCategories": [
      "RTC"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": [],
    "sourceOriginalAnswerKey": "9381 [C]",
    "sourceCorrection": "On p. 3-30 the printed key labels question 9831 as 9381. The printed choice C is retained and linked to the actual question number; the explanatory text is unchanged."
  },
