  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8877",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Airspace",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "What minimum aircraft equipment is required for operation within Class C airspace?",
    "options": [
      "Two-way communications.",
      "Two-way communications and transponder.",
      "Transponder and DME."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "An encoding transponder and two-way radio is required in order to operate within Class C airspace. (PLT040, AA.II.A.S6) — AIM ¶3-2-4 Answer (A) is incorrect because a Mode C transponder is also required. Answer (C) is incorrect because two-way communications are also required and DME is not required.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-8 · question 8877 · ALL",
