  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8878",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Airspace",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "What service is provided for aircraft operating within the outer area of Class C airspace?",
    "options": [
      "The same as within Class C airspace when communications and radar contact is established.",
      "Radar vectors to and from secondary airports within the outer area.",
      "Basic radar service only when communications and radar contact is established."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The same services are provided for aircraft operating within the outer area, as within the Class C airspace, when two-way communication and radar contact are established. (PLT161, AA.II.A.S6) — AIM ¶3-2-4 Answer (B) is incorrect because providing radar vectors to and from secondary airports within the outer circle is not a mandated service of ATC. Answer (C) is incorrect because the same services are provided in the outer area as within Class C airspace, once two-way communications and radar contact are established.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-8 · question 8878 · ALL",
