    "seccion": "Airspace",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "At what minimum altitude is a turbine-engine-powered, or large airplane, required to enter Class D airspace?",
    "options": [
      "1,500 feet AGL.",
      "2,000 feet AGL.",
      "2,500 feet AGL."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "When operating to an airport with an operating control tower, each pilot of a turbine-powered airplane or a large airplane shall, unless otherwise required by the applicable distance from cloud criteria, enter Class D airspace at an altitude of at least 1,500 feet above the surface of the airport. (PLT161, AA.I.G.K2) — 14 CFR §91.129",
