  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8262",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Alternate Airport Planning",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "An alternate airport is not required to dispatch a flag air carrier airplane for a flight of less than 6 hours when the visibility for at least 1 hour before and 1 hour after the ETA at the destination airport is forecast to be",
    "options": [
      "2 miles or greater.",
      "at least 3 miles, or 2 miles more than the lowest applicable minimum.",
      "3 miles."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "An alternate airport need not be listed if the destination weather, from one hour before to one hour after the ETA, is forecast to have the required ceiling criteria and the visibility is forecast to be at least 3 miles, or 2 miles more than the lowest visibility minimums, whichever is greater, for the instrument approach procedures to be used at the destination airport. (PLT379, AA.I.G.K4) — 14 CFR §121.621",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-18 · question 8262 · ATM, ADX",
