  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9790",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "ATC Clearances",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 241 and 242.) As you rolled out long on Runway 30 after landing at Long Beach (LGB), you slowed and turned left on very wide pavement and now see Taxiway D signs on both sides of your pavement. You notice your heading is about 250°. Tower is urging you to turn left on D, cross 16R/34L, then taxi to G and hold short of Runway 30. You now know you",
    "options": [
      "exited onto Runway 25R and transited HS 2.",
      "exited onto Taxiway G.",
      "exited at Taxiway J and transited HS 4."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The very wide pavement and taxiway D signs on both sides of the pavement indicate you are now on Runway 25R in the HS1 and HS2 region. (PLT149, AA.II.C.K3) — AIM ¶4-3-18",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-25 · question 9790 · ATM, ATS, RTC",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9790",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
