    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "When departing from an alternate airport within the United States which is not listed in the operations specifications, an air carrier must use the Part 97 takeoff minimums. When no takeoff minimums are specified, the air carrier must use a ceiling and visibility of 800-2, 900-1-1/2, or 1,000-1. (PLT380, AA.VI.B.K1) — 14 CFR §121.637",
