  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9827_3",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Takeoff Procedures",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "During takeoff roll with runway remaining, you receive a master caution light after V . What action R should you take?",
    "options": [
      "Reject the takeoff.",
      "Hold the nose down to takeoff speed.",
      "Continue the takeoff."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "VR is the speed at which the rotation of the aircraft should be initiated to takeoff attitude. cannot be less V R than V1. If it is greater than V1 and at it is found that, VR rotation cannot be achieved, a subsequent rejected takeoff may not be possible within the remaining runway length, and is likely to result in a runway excursion. In these circumstances, you should continue the takeoff. (PLT208, AA.VII.B.K1) — FAA-H-8083-3",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-28 · question 9827-3 · ATM, ADX",
