  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8858",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Holding",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "When using a flight director system, what rate of turn or bank angle should a pilot observe during turns in a holding pattern?",
    "options": [
      "3° per second or 25° bank, whichever is less.",
      "3° per second or 30° bank, whichever is less.",
      "1-1/2° per second or 25° bank, whichever is less."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "When making turns in the holding pattern, use whichever of the following requires the least angle of bank: 1. 3° per second; 2. 30° bank angle; or 3. 25° bank provided a flight director system is used. (PLT047, AA.VI.J.K1) — AIM ¶5-3-8",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-46 · question 8858 · ALL",
