    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Determine the holding pattern by placing your pencil on the holding fix and dragging it on the holding radial given by ATC, then returning back to the fix. Then draw the pattern from the fix with turns in the direction specified. Holding west on the 270° radial with right turns means you will be south of R-090. The entry procedure is based on the aircraft’s heading. To determine which entry procedure to use, draw a line at a 70° angle from the holding fix, and cutting the outbound leg at about one-third its length. With a heading of 055°, we are in the largest piece of pie, so a direct entry would be used. (PLT296, AA.VI.J.K1) — AIM ¶5-3-8 Answer (A) is incorrect because a parallel entry would be appropriate only from R-090 to R-200. Answer (C) is incorrect because a teardrop entry would only be appropriate from R-020 to R-090.",
