    "seccion": "Charts",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 192.) On the airway J10 between OBH and LBF, the MAA is 41,000 feet. What is the MAA on J197 between FSD and OBH?",
    "options": [
      "43,000 feet.",
      "45,000 feet.",
      "60,000 feet."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The MAA is the maximum usable altitude or flight level on an airway or jet route which has a published MEA. FL450 is the upper limit of all jet routes. (PLT100, AA.VI.C.K1) — Pilot/Controller Glossary Answer (A) is incorrect because the upper limit of the jet route system includes FL450 unless marked otherwise. Answer (C) is incorrect because this is the upper limit of Class A airspace, but the jet route system stops above 45,000 feet.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-52 · question 9644 · ALL",
