  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8784",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Charts",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 100, Area 8.) Where is the VOR changeover point on V571 between Navasota (TNV) and Humble (IAH)?",
    "options": [
      "24 miles from IAH.",
      "18 miles from IAH.",
      "Halfway between TNV and IAH"
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The changeover should be made at the changeover symbol if depicted, where there is a change in the direction of the airway, or in the absence of these at the halfway point between the VORs. In this case, the changeover point (COP) is indicated with a symbol, and the changeover should be made 24 miles from IAH and 18 miles from TNV. (PLT058, AA.VI.C.K1) — Enroute Low Altitude Chart Legend",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-54 · question 8784 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "8784",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
