  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8826",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Charts",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 114, Area 9.) What is the minimum altitude southwest bound on V8 at LUCER intersection?",
    "options": [
      "9,300 feet.",
      "9,000 feet.",
      "10,500 feet."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "The flag at LUCER intersection signifies a minimum crossing altitude of 9,300 feet for aircraft flying southwest along V8-21-282-587. The MEA on V8 SW at this intersection changes from 9,000 to 10,500 feet; aircraft must be at a minimum altitude of 9,300 feet when crossing. (PLT058, AA.VI.C.K1) — Enroute Low Altitude Chart Legend Answer (B) is incorrect because 9,000 feet is the MEA on V8 SW prior to reaching LUCER. Answer (C) is incorrect because 10,500 feet is the MEA on V8 SW after passing LUCER.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-55 · question 8826 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "8826",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 55,
