  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8852",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Charts",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 279 and Legend 72.) What is the approximate rate of descent required (for planning purposes) to maintain the electronic glide slope at 120 KIAS with a reported headwind component of 15 knots?",
    "options": [
      "637 ft/min.",
      "478 ft/min.",
      "558 ft/min."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "The ILS RWY 32R approach into Chicago-O’Hare has a 3° glide slope as indicated within the profile section of the approach chart. Using FAA Legend 72 along with a ground speed of 105 (120 KIAS — 15 knot headwind component), the rate of descent is 557.5 FPM. (PLT083, AA.VI.C.K1) — IFR Approach Procedures Answer (A) is incorrect because a rate of descent of 637 FPM is appropriate for the indicated airspeed of 120 knots. Answer (B) is incorrect because a rate of descent of 478 FPM is appropriate for a 3.0° glide slope angle at 90 knots.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-55 · question 8852 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "8852",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 55,
    "sourceCategories": [
      "ALL"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": [
      "atp_2026_figure-279-unit.svg",
      "atp_2026_legend-72-unit.svg"
    ]
  },
  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8852_1",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 6,
    "capituloTitulo": "Flight Operations",
    "seccion": "Charts",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Legend 72 and Figure 361.) With a speed of 140 knots, what is the minimum rate of climb after taking off from Rwy 3 at TUS to reach 9,900 feet? Interpolation required.",
    "options": [
      "963 FPM.",
      "1,065 FPM.",
      "930 FPM."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Using Figure 361, standard takeoff minimums for Runway 3 is 400 ft/NM. Using Legend 72 and the 140 knots provided in the question, interpolate the rate of climb by finding 400 ft/NM on the left-hand column and 140 knots on the top of the chart for the groundspeed. The minimum rate of climb is 963 FPM. (PLT058, AA.I.B.K2c) — FAA-H-8083-3 Answer (B) is incorrect because a minimum rate of climb of 1,065 FPM is for 425ft/NM at 150 knots. Answer (C) is incorrect because a minimum rate of climb of 930 FPM is for 370 ft/NM at 150 knots.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 6 Flight Operations · p. 6-55 · question 8852-1 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "8852-1",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
    "sourcePage": 55,
    "sourceCategories": [
      "ALL"
    ],
    "status": "publicada",
    "source": "import",
    "imagenes": [
      "atp_2026_figure-361-unit.svg",
      "atp_2026_legend-72-unit.svg"
    ]
  },
  {
