    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Arctic thundershowers, usually circumnavigable, move generally from northeast to southwest in the polar easterlies which is opposite from the general movement in mid-latitudes. (PLT495, AA.I.C.K3e) — FAA-H-8083-28",
