  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9240",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "The Atmosphere",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "What weather feature occurs at altitude levels near the tropopause?",
    "options": [
      "Maximum winds and narrow wind shear zones.",
      "Abrupt temperature increase above the tropopause.",
      "Thin layers of cirrus (ice crystal) clouds at the tropopause level."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Maximum winds generally occur at levels near the tropopause. These strong winds create narrow zones of wind shear which often generate hazardous turbulence. (PLT203, AA.I.C.K3a) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (B) is incorrect because temperature is fairly constant above the tropopause. Answer (C) is incorrect because thin layers of cirrus (ice crystal) clouds can develop at altitudes below the tropopause level and extend into the lower stratosphere.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-6 · question 9240 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9240",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
