    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "The Atmosphere",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Where is a common location for an inversion?",
    "options": [
      "At the tropopause.",
      "In the stratosphere.",
      "At the base of cumulus clouds."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Inversions are common in the stratosphere. (PLT203, AA.I.C.K3a) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (A) is incorrect because a common location for an inversion is in the stratosphere, not at the tropopause. Answer (C) is incorrect because the base of cumulus clouds is where the dew point lapse rate and the dry adiabatic lapse rate converge. It is not a common location for an inversion.",
