      "In a single continuous band, encircling the Earth, where there is a break between the equatorial and polar tropopause."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The jet stream is usually associated with a break in the tropopause where intensified temperature gradients are located. (PLT302, AA.I.C.K3a) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (A) is incorrect because a jet stream is located in a break in the tropopause, not in the stratosphere. Answer (C) is incorrect because there may be more than one jet stream at any time; up to three at one time are not uncommon.",
