  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9238",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "The Atmosphere",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Where do the maximum winds associated with the jetstream usually occur?",
    "options": [
      "In the vicinity of breaks in the tropopause on the polar side of the jet core.",
      "Below the jet core where a long straight stretch of the jetstream is located.",
      "On the equatorial side of the jetstream where moisture has formed cirriform clouds."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Maximum winds in a jet stream occur near a break in the tropopause and on the polar side. (PLT302, AA.I.C.K3b) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (B) is incorrect because in the jet stream, the maximum winds are found in, not below, the core. Answer (C) is incorrect because when moisture is available, cirriform clouds will form on the upward motion of air of the jet stream on the equatorial side. This will occur in the slower winds of the jet stream.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-7 · question 9238 · ALL",
