    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Development of a surface low is usually south of the jet stream. As the low deepens, it moves nearer the jet center. When a low occludes, the jet stream usually crosses the frontal system at the point of the occlusion. (PLT302, AA.I.C.K3e) — FAA-H-8083-28 Steep frontal surfaces are usually associated",
