  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9228_1",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Weather Systems",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "with",
    "options": [
      "fast moving warm front.",
      "fast moving cold front.",
      "dry lines."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "The leading edge of an advancing cold air mass is a cold front. Warm fronts on the surface are seldom as well marked as cold fronts, and they usually move about half as fast when the general wind flow is the same in each case. (PLT511, AA.I.C.K3e) — FAA-H-8083-28",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-10 · question 9228-1 · ALL",
