    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Fog and Rain",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "You are planning a flight to the West Coast of the United States, which is currently below the published weather minimums for an ILS approach to that airport. Winds are forecast to increase to above 20 knots from the west at your scheduled arrival time. What weather conditions should you expect?",
    "options": [
      "Visual meteorological conditions.",
      "Advection fog will deepen with winds above 20 knots.",
      "A layer of low stratus or stratocumulus is expected."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Advection fog is most common along coastal areas and will develop into a layer of stratus of stratocumulus clouds with wind speeds in excess of 15 knots. (PLT226, AA.I.C.K3j) — FAA-H-8083-28",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-16 · question 9206 · ALL",
