  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_8723",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Fog and Rain",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "A flight is scheduled at daybreak. The current weather is rainy but is expected to clear, with temperature/dew point spread forecast to be 10°C/10°C and winds 330° at 5 knots. What weather conditions should you expect?",
    "options": [
      "Visual meteorological conditions until later in the day.",
      "These conditions could produce radiation fog.",
      "Dense fog that deepens later in the day."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Conditions favorable for radiation fog are clear sky, little or no wind, and small temperature/dew point spread (high relative humidity). Radiation fog is restricted to land because water surfaces cool little from nighttime radiation. (PLT226, AA.I.C.K3j) — FAA-H-8083-28",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-17 · question 8723 · ALL",
