  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9196",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Thunderstorms",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Which weather phenomenon signals the beginning of the mature stage of a thunderstorm?",
    "options": [
      "The appearance of an anvil top.",
      "The start of rain at the surface.",
      "Growth rate of the cloud is at its maximum."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Precipitation beginning to fall from the cloud base is the indication that a downdraft has developed and a thunderstorm cell has entered the mature stage. (PLT495, AA.I.C.K3h) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (A) is incorrect because the appearance of an anvil top occurs during the dissipating stage. Answer (C) is incorrect because the growth rate of a thunderstorm is at its greatest during the cumulus stage.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-19 · question 9196 · ALL",
