  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9197",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Thunderstorms",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "During the life cycle of a thunderstorm, which stage is characterized predominately by downdrafts?",
    "options": [
      "Cumulus.",
      "Dissipating.",
      "Mature."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Downdrafts characterize the dissipating stage of the thunderstorm. (PLT495, AA.I.C.K3h) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (A) is incorrect because the cumulus stage is the building stage characterized by updrafts. Answer (C) is incorrect because the mature stage has both updrafts and downdrafts, which create strong wind shears.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-19 · question 9197 · ALL",
