    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Thunderstorms",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "What feature is normally associated with the cumulus stage of a thunderstorm?",
    "options": [
      "Beginning of rain at the surface.",
      "Frequent lightning.",
      "Continuous updraft."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "The key feature of the cumulus stage is a continuous updraft. (PLT495, AA.I.C.K3h) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (A) is incorrect because the beginning of rain at a surface marks the beginning of the mature stage. Answer (B) is incorrect because frequent lightning occurs after the downdrafts have developed and produce the static electricity which causes lightning.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-19 · question 9198 · ALL",
