  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9211",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Thunderstorms",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "A clear area in a line of thunderstorm echoes on a radar scope indicates",
    "options": [
      "the absence of clouds in the area.",
      "an area of no convective turbulence.",
      "an area where precipitation drops are not detected."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Airborne weather radar detects only precipitation size raindrops and hail. Absence of a radar return does indicate an area free of clouds or turbulence. (PLT495, AA.I.C.K3h) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (A) is incorrect because weather radar detects only precipitation drops, not clouds. Answer (B) is incorrect because convective turbulence, which would not be detected by radar, could be found under cumulus clouds. Radar does not detect turbulence.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-21 · question 9211 · ALL",
