    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Steady state thunderstorms usually are associated with weather systems. Fronts, converging winds, and troughs aloft force upward motion spawning these storms which often form into squall lines. Afternoon heating intensifies them. (PLT495, AA.I.C.K3h) — FAA-H-8083-28",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-22 · question 9835 · ALL",
