    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "With a headwind of 45 knots, the pilot may expect a total shear of 90 knots across the microburst. (PLT317, AA.I.C.K3h) — AIM ¶7-1-24 Answer (A) is incorrect because the total shear is the total headwind to tailwind change of a traversing airplane, thus a 45-knot headwind would shear 90 knots, not 40 knots, to a 45-knot tailwind. Answer (B) is incorrect because the total shear is the total headwind to tailwind change of a traversing airplane, thus a 45-knot headwind would shear 90 knots, not 80 knots, to a 45-knot tailwind.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-27 · question 9144 · ALL",
