  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9145",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Wind Shear",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 144.) If involved in a microburst encounter, in which aircraft positions will the most severe downdraft occur?",
    "options": [
      "4 and 5.",
      "2 and 3.",
      "3 and 4."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "An airplane flying through the microburst as depicted in FAA Figure 144 would encounter increasing performance in position 1, followed by a decreasing headwind in position 2. At position 3 the aircraft would encounter the strong downdraft followed by a strong tailwind at position 4. Position 5 represents the situation just before ground contact. (PLT317, AA.I.C.K3h) — AIM ¶7-1-24 Answer (A) is incorrect because position 5 has significantly less downdraft even though it has considerably more tailwind. Answer (B) is incorrect because position 2 has not as significant a downdraft as 3 and 4, but it contains a significant headwind even though it is decreasing.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-27 · question 9145 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9145",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
