  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9148",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Wind Shear",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "(Refer to Figure 144.) What effect will a microburst encounter have upon the aircraft in position 4?",
    "options": [
      "Strong tailwind.",
      "Strong updraft.",
      "Significant performance increase."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "An airplane flying through the microburst as depicted in FAA Figure 144 would encounter increasing performance in position 1, followed by a decreasing headwind in position 2. At position 3 the aircraft would encounter the strong downdraft followed by a strong tailwind at position 4. Position 5 represents the situation just before ground contact. (PLT317, AA.I.C.K3h) — AIM ¶7-1-24 Answer (B) is incorrect because updrafts will occur in thunderstorms, not in microbursts from thunderstorms. Answer (C) is incorrect because the significant increase in performance occurs at position 1 where the headwind component is the greatest.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-28 · question 9148 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9148",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
