  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9441",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Frost and Ice",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Which is a disadvantage of the one-step over the two-step process when deicing/anti-icing an airplane?",
    "options": [
      "It is more complicated.",
      "The holding time is increased.",
      "More fluid is used with the one-step method when large deposits of ice and snow must be flushed off airplane surfaces."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Use the two-stage process to remove ice deposits with hot water or a mix of FPD and water. This reduces the amount of fluid required. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 120-58 Answer (A) is incorrect because the one-step process is less complicated. Answer (B) is incorrect because one of the advantages of the one-step process is increased holding time.",
