  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9442",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Frost and Ice",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "The purpose of diluting ethylene glycol deicing fluid with water in non-precipitation conditions is to",
    "options": [
      "raise the eutectic point.",
      "decrease the freeze point.",
      "increase the minimum freezing point (onset of crystallization)."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Pure ethylene glycol will freeze at warmer temperatures than aqueous solutions of ethylene glycol. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 20-117 Answer (A) is incorrect because diluting ethylene glycol lowers the eutectic point. Answer (C) is incorrect because diluting ethylene glycol decreases the minimum freezing point (onset of crystallization).",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-32 · question 9442 · ALL",
