  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9444",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Frost and Ice",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Which of the following will decrease the holding time during anti-icing using a two-step process?",
    "options": [
      "Apply heated Type II fluid.",
      "Decrease the water content.",
      "Increase the viscosity of Type I fluid."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Heating fluids increases their deicing effectiveness; however, in the anti-icing process, unheated fluids are more effective. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 120-58 Answer (B) is incorrect because decreasing the water content will increase the holding time. Answer (C) is incorrect because increasing the viscosity of Type I fluid will increase the holding time.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-32 · question 9444 · ALL",
