    "explanation": "SAE and ISO Type 2 fluids contain a minimum of 50% glycols and are considered “thickened” because of added thickening agents that enable the fluid to be deposited in a thicker film and to remain on the aircraft surfaces until the time for takeoff. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 120-58",
