    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Frost and Ice",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Anti-icing fluid should provide freezing point protection to",
    "options": [
      "-20°F ambient temperature.",
      "+32°F outside temperature or below.",
      "a freezing point no greater than 20°F below the ambient or airplane surface temperature."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "In any case the freezing point of residual fluids (water, FPD fluids, or mixtures) should not be greater than 20°F below ambient or surface temperature, whichever is less. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 20-117 Answers (A) and (B) are incorrect because anti-icing fluid should protect from icing to a freezing point no greater than 20°F below the ambient or aircraft surface temperature.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-34 · question 9448 · ALL",
