  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9450",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Frost and Ice",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Freezing Point Depressant (FPD) fluids used for deicing",
    "options": [
      "provide ice protection during flight.",
      "are intended to provide ice protection on the ground only.",
      "on the ground, cause no performance degradation during takeoff."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "FPD fluids are used to aid the ground deicing process and provide a protective film to delay formations of frost, snow, or other ice. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 120-58 Answer (A) is incorrect because FPD does not provide inflight protection. Answer (C) is incorrect because some large aircraft experience performance degradation and may require weight or other compensation.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-34 · question 9450 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9450",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
