    "seccion": "Frost and Ice",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Freezing Point Depressant (FPD) fluids are highly soluble in water; however,",
    "options": [
      "ice is slow to absorb it but fast to melt when in contact with FPD.",
      "ice absorbs it very fast but is slow to melt when in contact with it.",
      "ice is slow to absorb it, and to melt when in contact with it."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "FPD fluids are highly soluble in water; however, ice is slow to absorb FPD or to melt when in contact with it. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 120-58 Answer (A) is incorrect because FPD fluids are slow to melt. Answer (B) is incorrect because FPD fluids are slow to absorb.",
