    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Frost and Ice",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Freezing Point Depressant (FPD) fluid residue on engine fan or compressor blades",
    "options": [
      "can increase performance and cause stalls or surges.",
      "could cause FPD vapors to enter the aircraft but would have no affect on engine thrust or power.",
      "can reduce engine performance and cause surging and/or compressor stalls."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 2,
    "explanation": "Fluid residue on engine fan or compressor blades can reduce engine performance or cause stall or surge. (PLT108, AA.I.B.K7) — AC 120-58 Answer (A) is incorrect because fluid residue would cause a decrease in performance. Answer (B) is incorrect because fluid residue would have an affect on engine thrust or power.",
