    "explanation": "For structural icing to occur, two conditions must be present: the aircraft must be flying through visible water such as rain or cloud droplets, and temperature at the point where the moisture strikes the aircraft must be 0° or colder. (PLT274, AA.I.C.K3i) — FAA-H-8083-28",
