      "Low stratus."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Mountain waves can generate standing lenticular clouds and rotor clouds. Of these, the rotor cloud is likely to be the lowest. (PLT501, AA.I.C.K3f) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (B) is incorrect because the standing lenticular clouds mark the crest, or the top, of each standing wave. Answer (C) is incorrect because low stratus clouds are not associated with a mountain wave.",
