  {
    "id": "q_la_ATP_2026_9777",
    "fuente": "ATP",
    "capitulo": 8,
    "capituloTitulo": "Meteorology and Weather Services",
    "seccion": "Turbulence",
    "materia": "operaciones",
    "text": "Clear air turbulence associated with a jet stream is",
    "options": [
      "most commonly found in temperatures between -40 and -50°C.",
      "most commonly found in the vicinity of the tropopause.",
      "similar to that associated with a tropical maritime front."
    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "Maximum winds generally occur at levels near the tropopause. These strong winds create narrow zones of wind shear which often generate hazardous turbulence. (PLT501, AA.I.C.K3g) — FAA-H-8083-28 Answer (A) is incorrect because temperatures are not a primary factor for CAT. Answer (C) is incorrect because CAT is associated with the tropopause, not a tropical maritime front.",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-40 · question 9777 · ALL",
    "sourceQuestionId": "9777",
    "sourceEdition": "2025–2026",
