    ],
    "correctIndex": 1,
    "explanation": "In addition to the information automatically included in an AWOS report, information can be manually added. The remarks are limited to thunderstorms (type and intensity), and obstructions to vision when the visibility is 3 SM or less. Augmentation is identified in the observation as “observer weather.” (PLT515, AA.I.C.K2) — AIM ¶7-1-10",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-46 · question 9704 · ALL",
