    ],
    "correctIndex": 0,
    "explanation": "Heights of the specified pressure for each station are analyzed through the use of solid lines called contours. This contour analysis gives the charts a height pattern. The contours depict highs, lows, troughs, and ridges, and all heights are given as pressure altitude. (PLT283, AA.I.C.K2) — FAA-H-8083-28",
    "cite": "ASA Airline Transport Pilot Test Prep 2025–2026 · Chapter 8 Meteorology and Weather Services · p. 8-48 · question 9281 · ALL",
